    "updated_at": "2026-02-03T04:24:50Z",
    "body": "I had a similar concern whereby I only expect aws context to be presented on my prompt **while my aws session is authenticated and active**, so I created a lightweight service for this purpose.\nCheck it out here: https://github.com/quaintops/starship-aws-monitor\n\nThe built-in Starship `[aws]` module shows AWS info even when credentials are expired. This service solves that by:\n\n- Running as a background systemd service (near-zero prompt latency)\n- Checking authentication via STS `GetCallerIdentity` every 60 seconds\n- Writing status to `~/.aws/auth-status` for Starship to read\n- Only displaying AWS info when actually authenticated\n\nCurrently supports systemd only; macOS launchd plist support can be added easily. So far tested mainly with AWS SSO and bash on Debian & Ubuntu.",
